/**

\page tarch_plotting Plotting

The classes in `tarch/plotter` write unstructured meshes and their fields. A
caller fills a tarch::plotter::Mesh with the points, the cells and the fields of
its rank and passes the mesh to tarch::plotter::FileWriter::write().

## File writers

A file writer writes the snapshots of one plot series. Every rank calls write()
for every snapshot at the same time. The function
tarch::plotter::createFileWriter() creates the writer of a format.

- The class tarch::plotter::VTUFileWriter writes one `.vtu` file per rank, one
  `.pvtu` file per snapshot and one `.pvd` file that lists the snapshots.
- The class tarch::plotter::VTKHDFFileWriter appends every snapshot as a step to
  one `.vtkhdf` file.
- The class tarch::plotter::HDF5FileWriter writes one `.h5` file and one `.xmf`
  file per snapshot and one `.xmf` file that embeds the grids of all snapshots.
- The class tarch::plotter::NetCDFFileWriter writes one UGRID file per snapshot
  and one `.nc.series` file that lists the snapshots.

## Parallel plotting

The VTKHDF, HDF5 and NetCDF writers write the meshes of all ranks into one file
through MPI-IO. Every rank passes a mesh with the same fields. The global master
writes the files that list the snapshots.

*/
